CORE PROMPT (Constraint-Weighted Procedural Prompting)

Style & Intent
A monumental, fate-driven choral orchestral score that feels ancient, inevitable, and merciless. Pagan ritual meets cinematic apocalypse. No tenderness. No hope. Only cycle.

Tempo & Meter
~108 BPM
Heavy 3/1–3/4 hybrid feel (slow triple pulse, massive downbeats)
Harmony & Tonality
D minor center (dark modal gravity)
Static harmonic mass — power comes from rhythm + density, not chord movement
Chords hit like verdicts, not progressions

🥁 RHYTHM & PERCUSSION (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
Massive taiko-style low drums
Gran casa hits that feel like collapsing stone
Timpani rolls swelling into impact
Percussion leads the fear, not the melody

Rule:
❌ No swing
❌ No groove
✅ Only ritual pulse

🎺 ORCHESTRATION
Full orchestra locked in block motion
Brass: short, brutal stabs (no heroism)
Strings: aggressive tremolo + unison attacks
Choir treated as a percussive force

🗣️ CHOIR (CRITICAL)
Large mixed choir (men dominant)
Latin phonemes, hard consonants
Shouted unison → sudden silence → shouted again
Dynamics jump from whispered dread to violent proclamation
Emotional tone:
“The universe does not care — and it never did.”

📐 STRUCTURE (CYCLE LAW)
Silence
Sudden impact (full ensemble)
Relentless repetition
Brief collapse
Return — louder, heavier
End without resolution

Rule:
⚠️ Must feel like it could loop forever
🎬 CINEMATIC USE CASE
Perfect for:
Apocalyptic reveals
Final boss emergence
Civilization collapse
“Fate has chosen” moments

Sora hyper-kinetic montages with no mercy cuts
🧠 CWPP ANCHOR PHRASE
“A merciless choral engine driven by ritual percussion and immutable fate — overwhelming, cyclical, and inescapable.”